                        <field name="dc_description">This is a careful copy of Hilary’s De fide sive de trinitate with a page with a decorative ‬initial‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬. The manuscript is listed in the All Saints Abbey register of books from about 1100 (Min. 17, f. 306v). In the 15th century this codex, like many others, received a new leather ‬‬‬binding‬‬ with metal bosses and two clasps. Fragments from the same 13th century as with Min. 39‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬‬ were used as ‬pastedowns. In addition, a ‬bifolium‬‬‬‬‬‬‬ from a manuscript of prayers was bound into the front. </field>
